# EUReadySeller Content Factory and GSC Workflow

EUReadySeller updates must follow the Content Factory system.

## Page creation rules
- Do not randomly create detached pages.
- Every new page must have:
  - user intent category
  - target queries
  - page template
  - primary keyword
  - secondary keywords
  - long-tail questions
  - required internal links
  - sitemap inclusion
  - llms.txt inclusion
  - canonical trailing slash
  - GSC submission recommendation
- Prefer one focused page per sprint.

## Current strategy
- Current EPR pages are growing and should not be repeatedly edited unless GSC data supports it.
- Use GSC and Semrush signals to guide page priority and wording.
- Avoid over-editing pages already showing growth.

## Next roadmap
- `/weee-registration-germany/`
- `/eu-batteries-regulation-for-sellers/`

## Content maintenance
- Keep Content Factory metadata in sync with page content, routes, and internal links.
- Use cautious wording and preserve SEO semantics.
- Only update a page when there is a clear search-intent or GSC reason.
